# strategies/

Drop `.qkt` files in this directory. They're mounted into the running daemon at
`/strategies` (read-only).

Bybit symbols use the prefix of their gateway broker entry: `BYBIT_LINEAR:` (linear
perpetual futures, the `bybit_linear` entry) or `BYBIT_SPOT:` (spot, the `bybit_spot`
entry). Examples:

```
SYMBOLS
    btc = BYBIT_LINEAR:BTCUSDT EVERY 5m WARMUP 50 BARS
    eth = BYBIT_SPOT:ETHUSDT EVERY 1m WARMUP 21 BARS
```

To deploy one:

```bash
make deploy STRAT=ema_cross
```

That runs `qkt deploy /strategies/ema_cross.qkt --as ema_cross` inside the
container. The daemon registers it and starts evaluating rules on the next tick.

After editing a deployed strategy, validate and replace only that running name:

```bash
make resync-dry-run STRAT=ema_cross
make resync STRAT=ema_cross
```

`resync` keeps unrelated strategies running. If validation or reconciliation
fails, the previous strategy remains registered.
Run `make reconcile STRAT=ema_cross` after live replacements to compare qkt's
ledger with the broker/account view.

To stop one:

```bash
make stop STRAT=ema_cross
```

The gateway trades Bybit testnet until you set `BYBIT_ENVIRONMENT=mainnet` and
`BYBIT_TRADE_MODE=real` in `.env` and run `make up` again.

Scaffolded by qkt v{{QKT_VERSION}}.
